I did not add the per-call enrichment fetch to `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=...`. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, so calling it would require importing `http-client`, which is authority the node doesn't have. The request would also send untrusted item text to an external host. The build fix is just removing the duplicate `use crate::{Classification, FeedItem};` line, since wit-bindgen already puts those names at the crate root.

